{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_hemosight_project", "label": "HemoSight project", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Non-invasive anemia screening from conjunctiva photographs and fingertip PPG; research project first, deployable product second. Contribution became the body of negative results and their mechanisms."}, {"id": "claude_core_scientific_bet", "label": "Core bet: photograph as spectroscopic measurement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Treat the photo as a spectroscopic measurement, not pixels for a CNN: recover reflectance from RGB, unmix into chromophores, report Hb in g/dL with calibrated uncertainty. Every design decision answerable to this bet."}, {"id": "claude_n1_calibration_free", "label": "N1: Calibration-free spectral super-resolution (sclera white reference)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "REFUTED Phase 2.5: sclera and specular references both lose to grey-world (6.076 dE2000 vs 7.427/7.821). Contribution became the diagnosis plus the recommendation of grey-world on a tight periocular crop."}, {"id": "claude_n1a_illuminant_accuracy", "label": "N1a: Illuminant estimation accuracy across sensors", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Validated on nus8, 6 cameras; colorchecker masked out to avoid leaking the answer. Survives intact."}, {"id": "claude_n1b_sclera_white_reference", "label": "N1b: Sclera as endogenous white reference across devices", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Self-consistency protocol on MOBIUS: no Hb labels needed, which is why the only device-diverse datasets can be used. Partially supported - negative on the headline."}, {"id": "claude_n1c_end_to_end_hb", "label": "N1c: Sclera-referenced correction improves Hb end to end", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eyes-Defy only: 218 subjects, 2 sites, one Samsung S6 model, no severe cases. Never reported without those numbers."}, {"id": "claude_n2_monte_carlo_forward_model", "label": "N2: Monte Carlo forward model of layered eyelid tissue", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Justification corrected 2026-09-11: purpose is label trustworthiness (only real severe cases carry contradictory labels), not data quantity. Full MC never built; a diffusion model sufficed to fail the Phase 3 gate."}, {"id": "claude_n3_physical_interpretability", "label": "N3: Physical interpretability (Hb in g/dL, chromophore maps)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Output a physical quantity and chromophore concentration maps rather than class probability and saliency. Superseded: no estimator survived the gates."}, {"id": "claude_n4_conformal_abstention", "label": "N4: Conformal prediction with selective abstention", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three-state output (negative / refer / cannot decide). Not applicable: wrapping conformal intervals around a model that loses to sex alone would calibrate a number nobody should use."}, {"id": "claude_n5_mechanistic_fairness_audit", "label": "N5: Mechanistic fairness audit (ITA, melanin vs illuminant)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rebuilt without SCIN on Individual Typology Angle; limitations: no ground-truth skin tone, ITA is a proxy, tone confounded with site. Mechanism measured in Phase 3 Task 4: melanin 0.005 shifts recovered Hb by +9.6 g/dL."}, {"id": "claude_n6_multimodal_fusion", "label": "N6: Multimodal fusion with graceful degradation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scoped: real fusion is conjunctiva+nail classification only (Ghana pool binary labels); image+PPG fusion is simulation-only permanently because no participants are shared. No palm dataset ever existed."}, {"id": "claude_hard_constraints", "label": "Hard constraints (public data only, retrospective, cross-site honesty, CNN baseline)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Public datasets only; never clinical validation; single-site numbers worthless; a conventional CNN baseline must be maintained for every claim; data/raw read-only; patient-level site-aware splits."}, {"id": "claude_working_protocol", "label": "Working protocol (append-only logs, tick on artefact)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never delete a log entry, supersede it; tick only when output exists on disk; CLAUDE.md capped at 120k chars by test; decisions/results/corrections go to docs/archive."}, {"id": "claude_dataset_nus8", "label": "NUS-8 colour constancy benchmark", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "6 of 8 cameras extracted, 1265 images with ground-truth illuminants. Validates N1a. Only 2 of 6 cameras have measured spectral sensitivities."}, {"id": "claude_dataset_sbvpi", "label": "SBVPI sclera dataset", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "High-res periocular studio captures; no Hb. Sclera segmentation, vessel ground truth, and the studio residual (1.06 dE2000) in Phase 7."}, {"id": "claude_dataset_mobius", "label": "MOBIUS mobile sclera dataset", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "3 phones x 3 lighting x 100 subjects recoverable from filenames; no Hb. The N1b self-consistency and N5 device axis."}, {"id": "claude_dataset_cp_anemic", "label": "CP-AnemiC (Ghana conjunctival pallor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hb labels REJECTED: 90 of 91 exact-duplicate groups carry conflicting Hb values; 87.3% byte-identical to Ghana conjunctiva files. Binary label only."}, {"id": "claude_dataset_ghana_conjunctiva", "label": "Ghana conjunctiva (Mendeley nt7r8hv2pz)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Superset containing CP-AnemiC; pre-segmented cutouts with no sclera; binary label only."}, {"id": "claude_dataset_ghana_fingernails", "label": "Ghana fingernails (Mendeley 2xx4j3kjg2)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shares a participant roster with Ghana conjunctiva (Jaccard 1.000, ~454 paired subjects); N6 evidence, binary only."}, {"id": "claude_dataset_eyes_defy_anemia", "label": "Eyes-Defy-Anemia (dataset anemia, India + Italy)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "218 subjects (95 India, 123 Italy), full photographs plus palpebral masks, Hb in per-site xlsx. The ONLY cross-site Hb imaging data; 217 trusted rows; one image per subject so within-subject residual not measurable."}, {"id": "claude_dataset_hb_ppg", "label": "Hb_PPG_Dataset (four-wavelength PPG, 252 subjects)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "660/730/850/940 nm, 200 Hz, 60 s, venous HemoCue reference. Promoted to co-primary because the LEDs are the illuminant so the illuminant-estimation error that killed imaging does not exist; still found NOT VIABLE."}, {"id": "claude_scin_deleted", "label": "SCIN (scin-main) - deleted, no data", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Held 5 documentation files; dermatology imagery with no conjunctiva, Hb or participant overlap, so its skin-tone labels could not attach to any subject. N5 rebuilt on ITA."}, {"id": "claude_ghana_pool_overlap_verdict", "label": "Ghana pool participant overlap verdict (CP-AnemiC inside Ghana conjunctiva)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "419 shared MD5 hashes, 98.2% within pHash Hamming 10: permanently one site; no split may place one in train and the other in test."}, {"id": "claude_grey_world_periocular_crop", "label": "Grey-world on a tight periocular crop (recommended normalisation)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Improves as field of view narrows (6.076 to 3.935 dE2000 at 25% FOV) because a wide frame is skin-dominated. The normalisation every later phase uses."}, {"id": "claude_phase_0_scaffold", "label": "Phase 0: Scaffold", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_phase_1_data_audit", "label": "Phase 1: Data audit, manifests, overlap check, splits", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Findings superseded scaffold-time guesses: dataset anemia IS Eyes-Defy; Ghana sets are one dataset with no sclera; SCIN empty."}, {"id": "claude_phase_1_5_remediation", "label": "Phase 1.5: Remediation of Phase 1 findings", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Restructured N1 into N1a/b/c, rejected Ghana Hb labels via hb_label_trusted, corrected N2, rebuilt N5, scoped N6, untracked figures."}, {"id": "claude_phase_2_sclera_illuminant", "label": "Phase 2: Sclera segmentation and illuminant estimation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sclera loses to grey-world p~3e-8. Diagnosis attributed failure to inter-individual reflectance variance, later found INCOMPLETE."}, {"id": "claude_phase_2_5_specular_rescue", "label": "Phase 2.5: Corneal specular highlight rescue (time-boxed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dichromatic model: specular reflection carries the illuminant SPD with no per-subject reflectance term. REFUTED: no better than sclera (p=0.29), so reflectance variance is not the sole limiting factor."}, {"id": "claude_phase_3_simulator_gate", "label": "Phase 3: Monte Carlo simulator and Task 0 gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gate: propagate grey-world's measured residual through the forward model. Result 3.893 g/dL at 3.935 dE2000 vs >2.0 threshold: NOT RECOVERABLE. Signal 0.84 dE2000/g/dL vs 3.9 noise = 4.7x."}, {"id": "claude_phase_3_5_ratio_reformulation", "label": "Phase 3.5: Within-image ratio reformulation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Von Kries ratio cancels the illuminant algebraically, needs only a per-subject stable reference. REFUTED at 10.04 g/dL equivalent (5x threshold): the sclera reference is noisier within-subject than between (1.447)."}, {"id": "claude_phase_4_imaging_n3_superseded", "label": "Phase 4 (imaging): Spectral reconstruction - SUPERSEDED", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every item presupposes the synthetic library never built and an inversion the gate showed cannot survive calibration error."}, {"id": "claude_phase_4_ppg_gates", "label": "Phase 4: PPG arm, Gate A and Gate B", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gate A: AC/DC fails to cancel nuisance variance on real data. Gate B: R2 -0.025, permutation p=0.978; NOT VIABLE. Task 3: sex alone MAE 0.831 beats PPG by 30%."}, {"id": "claude_phase_4_5_deep_ppg", "label": "Phase 4.5: Deep models on raw PPG", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Closes the last untested representation. Best MAE 1.113 vs sex alone 0.831; but the raw waveform does carry a real signal (spectrogram CNN z=-4.72), ~0.05 g/dL better than a constant."}, {"id": "claude_phase_5_harden_consolidate", "label": "Phase 5: Harden the positive claim and consolidate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Selection-aware permutation with best-of-six inside each permutation; extended to n=240: empirical p <= 0.0041 (a floor), z=-4.96, seed SD 0.0069, gap 11.9x seed SD."}, {"id": "claude_phase_6_audit_harness", "label": "Phase 6: HemoSight Audit harness (software deliverable)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The shippable product is the methodological audit pipeline the gates were run with, generalised to any screening model's predictions. Eight checks returning PASS/FAIL/INSUFFICIENT DATA; replaces the original conformal Phase 6 for sequencing only."}, {"id": "claude_phase_6_5_closure", "label": "Phase 6.5: Closure of outstanding audit items", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measured empirical signal 0.84 (withdrew 0.70 constant); built the image CNN baseline (MAE 1.301 vs site+sex+age 1.273); ran Phase 5 checks end to end; verified licences."}, {"id": "claude_phase_7_additions", "label": "Phase 7: Controlled capture, statistical-vs-clinical, external audit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Controlled-capture hypothesis outcome B: studio residual 1.06 dE2000 gives gate MAE 1.04, MARGINAL; VIABLE needs <0.99, achieved by no condition. External audit: 0 of 3 candidates auditable."}, {"id": "claude_phase_8a_dual_audience_language", "label": "Phase 8A: Audit tool language for a dual audience", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Layered disclosure: plain language default, technical statement one click away, never removed. Simplify the sentence, never the claim. What-to-do is exactly FIXABLE / REPORT IT / STOP."}, {"id": "claude_phase_8b_visual_redesign", "label": "Phase 8B: Visual redesign (dark instrument)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No stock photography and nothing derived from a dataset image; every visual generated from tabulated physics or the project's own aggregate results. Lighthouse 97-100."}, {"id": "claude_phase_9a_screening_reframe", "label": "Phase 9A: Screening reframe (triage task)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The product delivers a referral decision, not a g/dL estimate, so refutation is tested on the product's own terms. Pre-declared: WHO adult thresholds, operating point = max specificity at sensitivity >= 0.90 chosen on training folds, margin >= 0.10 with CI lower bound > 0, 2000 bootstrap resamples. Imaging WEAKENED within site, CONFIRMED cross-site; PPG CONFIRMED."}, {"id": "claude_phase_6_orig_conformal_superseded", "label": "Phase 6 (original): Conformal prediction - SUPERSEDED", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_phase_7_orig_fairness_superseded", "label": "Phase 7 (original): Fairness audit - SUPERSEDED", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_phase_8_orig_fusion_superseded", "label": "Phase 8 (original): Multimodal fusion - SUPERSEDED", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_phase_9_web_app_superseded", "label": "Phase 9: Web application - SUPERSEDED", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_phase_10_flutter_superseded", "label": "Phase 10: Flutter mobile - SUPERSEDED", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_imaging_arm_closed_final", "label": "Verdict: imaging arm CLOSED, FINAL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four representations refuted with mechanisms. A decision not to build further, not a claim the image carries no information: within site it moves a referral threshold; the binding reason is cross-site collapse (sensitivity 0.397)."}, {"id": "claude_ppg_arm_not_viable", "label": "Verdict: PPG arm NOT VIABLE", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Negative R2, sex alone beats it by 30%; Phase 9A: AUROC diff vs demographics -0.000, NNS 15.8 vs 14.0 for referring everybody."}, {"id": "claude_sex_alone_benchmark", "label": "Benchmark: sex alone, MAE 0.831 g/dL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No method across two modalities beat a single binary demographic variable; exposes how an apparently working estimator is really a sex classifier."}, {"id": "claude_site_sex_age_baseline", "label": "Baseline: site + sex + age (MAE 1.273, AUROC 0.816)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The benchmark to beat on the imaging screening task; site was omitted from a first run and corrected."}, {"id": "claude_one_positive_claim_spectrogram_cnn", "label": "The one positive claim: raw-PPG spectrogram CNN (real, useless)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "z=-4.96, empirical p <= 0.0041 (a floor 1/(n+1), not a measurement); improves on a constant by ~0.05 g/dL; separates no WHO band. Writing 'deep learning found nothing' would be false; 'worked' far more false."}, {"id": "claude_conventional_cnn_baseline", "label": "Conventional CNN baseline (ResNet-18 on Eyes-Defy, MAE 1.301)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Section 3 hard constraint met in Phase 6.5; MARGINAL; cross-site italy_to_india 1.96, india_to_italy 1.99."}, {"id": "claude_mean_cielab_ridge_model", "label": "Mean palpebral CIELAB + ridge (strongest within-site screening model)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three numbers match the CNN on AUROC (0.874 vs 0.875) and beat it on specificity at matched sensitivity (0.752 vs 0.656); +0.192 specificity over site+sex+age, CI [+0.114,+0.276]. Any future imaging work should start here, not from a CNN."}, {"id": "claude_moves_no_clinical_threshold_retired", "label": "Retired phrase: 'moves no clinical threshold'", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phase 7 claim contradicted by Phase 9A: within site the image cuts referral rate 0.634 to 0.519 at ~0.90 detection. Mirror-image of the literature's error: a baseline comparison on a metric the product does not use."}, {"id": "claude_plug_in_operating_point_artefact", "label": "Plug-in operating point artefact (PPG sensitivity 0.00)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Refer if predicted Hb below threshold: regression shrinks toward the mean so this is systematically insensitive; measures the rule as much as the model. At a screening point sensitivity 0.889 but specificity 0.098."}, {"id": "claude_tech_stack", "label": "Tech stack (Python 3.12, PyTorch CUDA, FastAPI, React/Vite, RTX 4060 8GB)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PyTorch must come from the cu126 index because PyPI serves CPU-only on Windows; 8 GB VRAM is a design constraint capping batch size and backbone."}, {"id": "claude_the_archive", "label": "docs/archive evidentiary record", "file